## Scope

R10-P1 only: deterministic, evidence-backed Recommended Actions on the privileged Home Command Center.

## Design locked first

Adds `docs/checkpoints/M-2026-11-01-R10-P1-Episode-Design-v1.md` before implementation.

## Database foundation

Adds `20261101162000_r10_command_center_recommendation_episodes_v1.sql`:

- tenant-scoped persistent episode state for exactly four CRM signals;
- canonical candidate view aligned to current Home/CRM evidence;
- oldest-first deterministic target ranking;
- overdue task baseline kept separate from deduplicated Lead targets;
- privileged, tenant-derived, concurrency-safe episode resolver;
- new episode only after a previously observed clear state;
- missing clear observations never fabricate recurrence;
- signal clear expires only untouched active recommendations for that episode;
- no recommendation rows are created by the migration itself.

## Presentation boundary

Adds POST `/api/intelligence/recommendations/present`:

- same-origin guard;
- authenticated workspace required;
- owner/admin/manager required;
- no client-supplied organization authority;
- 50-Lead bounded working set;
- uses only reply backlog, overdue follow-up, first-touch and payment-pending facts;
- suppresses non-active/terminal current-episode recommendations;
- calls hardened P0 v2 touch only for recommendations returned for display;
- private/no-store response;
- no stale event-intelligence predictions or predictive probabilities.

## Home UI

Adds a separate Recommended Actions client panel through the existing privileged Home layout. Existing factual Home/Attention cards are unchanged.

The UI explicitly states:

- deterministic CRM guidance;
- observed evidence;
- priority score is ordering only, not conversion probability.

No Accept/Dismiss/Start/Complete controls are introduced in P1.

## Regression protection

Adds `verify:r10-command-center-recommendations-v1` to the production build.

## Safety

- no AI-generated recommendation prose;
- no autonomous external/customer/provider action;
- no predictive-model activation;
- no recommendation/outcome seed data;
- production recommendation evidence will begin only when a real privileged Home user invokes the presentation panel after deployment.

