## What this plans

`docs/plans/07-fallback-closes.md`, part 1 of stage 7: the facilitator's **sponsored close** and **scenario 15**. A buyer that holds no SOL and has no node access can close its session through the facilitator.

| Task | Builds |
|---|---|
| 1 | The `closeUrl` wire in the scheme: `CloseInfo` (the body of `GET /close`), `readCloseInfo`, `storedSessionFields`, and `buildSponsoredClose`, which refuses a body that describes another session or another authority |
| 2 | `apps/facilitator/src/close.ts`: `GET /close`'s body, with a cached blockhash; `verifySponsoredClose` (spec 5.4, sponsored row, static checks first); `createSponsoredCloser`, which settles one close at a time per session |
